  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43341034",
      "title": "Configuring CSS For Images With The \"fill\" Prop",
      "lectureOrder": 199,
      "videoOrder": 185,
      "sourceHash": "a73299b93bb8c0bc205f58ab14806c6be9c552b26311ceef9c685c8342de4927",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.51,
          "end": 3.12,
          "en": "So why do images that are loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.12,
          "end": 6.24,
          "en": "with help of the next/image and that fill prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.24,
          "end": 9.69,
          "en": "take up the entire available screen space?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.69,
          "end": 13.08,
          "en": "Well, because the fill prop essentially tells NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.08,
          "end": 16.8,
          "en": "that we don't know the exact size of the loaded image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.8,
          "end": 19.86,
          "en": "and that if they offer, should fill up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.86,
          "end": 23.79,
          "en": "all the space it can get, and by default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.79,
          "end": 27.21,
          "en": "if you don't have any other settings, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.21,
          "end": 30.09,
          "en": "that will be the entire screen space.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.09,
          "end": 32.37,
          "en": "Now, that's, of course, not what we want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.37,
          "end": 34.14,
          "en": "and therefore, what you should do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.14,
          "end": 37.65,
          "en": "when you're using the next/image with the fill prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.65,
          "end": 41.79,
          "en": "is you should go to the container element of that image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.79,
          "end": 45.66,
          "en": "or add such a container element if you don't have one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.66,
          "end": 50.43,
          "en": "and change the CSS style settings on that container.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.43,
          "end": 54.262,
          "en": "So in my case, I need to change the CSS styles of that div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.262,
          "end": 56.973,
          "en": "that has the class name post-image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.87,
          "end": 60.33,
          "en": "Now, I can do that here in my project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.33,
          "end": 64.26,
          "en": "in the app folder in the globals.css file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.26,
          "end": 66.87,
          "en": "There, if you scroll down, at some point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.87,
          "end": 71.87,
          "en": "you'll find this post and post-image styling here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 73.23,
          "end": 76.14,
          "en": "and I'll add a new rule here where I target the element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.14,
          "end": 77.883,
          "en": "with the class post-image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.9,
          "end": 83.76,
          "en": "And what you should do when using this fill prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.76,
          "end": 88.76,
          "en": "is you should set the parent container, so the container",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 88.856,
          "end": 91.8,
          "en": "in which you're using the next/image component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 91.8,
          "end": 95.163,
          "en": "to have a position of relative,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 97.02000000000001,
          "end": 99.66,
          "en": "because this fill prop here will, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 99.66,
          "end": 102.24000000000001,
          "en": "set the position of the image element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 102.24000000000001,
          "end": 104.1,
          "en": "that's rendered to absolute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 104.1,
          "end": 106.56,
          "en": "and that, in turn, will then position the element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.56,
          "end": 108.57,
          "en": "in the closest parent container",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.57,
          "end": 112.11,
          "en": "that has a position of relative, or some other position,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.11,
          "end": 114.12299999999999,
          "en": "but relative is the common choice here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.44,
          "end": 116.936,
          "en": "Now if you do that, you'll therefore see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.936,
          "end": 120.09,
          "en": "that now there are no images at all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.09,
          "end": 122.501,
          "en": "and the reason for that is that when using that fill prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.501,
          "end": 126.6,
          "en": "NextJS will position the image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 126.6,
          "end": 130.41,
          "en": "according to the container element's position element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 130.41,
          "end": 132.597,
          "en": "and it will take up all the width and height",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.597,
          "end": 135.6,
          "en": "determined by the container.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 135.6,
          "end": 137.82,
          "en": "So what you must do in such a case here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.82,
          "end": 142.38,
          "en": "is set a width and height on the container element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 142.38,
          "end": 146.1,
          "en": "So here, I was setting width and height with CSS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 146.1,
          "end": 147.84,
          "en": "on the image element itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 147.84,
          "end": 150.903,
          "en": "That should now instead move to the container element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 152.52,
          "end": 155.737,
          "en": "And with that done, you see the images are now loaded again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 155.737,
          "end": 158.913,
          "en": "and they are displayed properly again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.81,
          "end": 163.8,
          "en": "but now they're also optimized by NextJS as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.8,
          "end": 166.382,
          "en": "as far as NextJS can optimize them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 166.382,
          "end": 169.26,
          "en": "and I'll get back to that in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 169.26,
          "end": 170.55,
          "en": "But you see that, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.55,
          "end": 173.31,
          "en": "this lazy loading property is again added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 173.31,
          "end": 175.44,
          "en": "and you see that the source set is set,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 175.44,
          "end": 180.44,
          "en": "so that can be useful, but that's not all I wanna do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.45,
          "end": 181.293,
          "en": "Indeed.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
